{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793482192,"nonce":"ovwErzD9YCk8CZnqzxJBndNnVAU=","title":"cn switch off snapped: a transform transition dropped the translation, and a hovered element's restyle was not eased","message":"Reported from a screen recording. Turning a switch off moved the thumb to the start in one frame, at mouse-down, and the track went from blue to grey in one frame at release.\n\nTwo causes in blinc_layout. (1) Pressing a checked switch changes only the thumb's scale; the transition then carried only the scale fields and the writer rebuilt the whole transform from them, dropping translateX. The thumb jumped at press and had nothing left to slide on release. The writer also composed scale before translate, so the pressed translation was 18px, not 20. (2) apply_complex_selector_styles skipped transition detection for a node that held a pointer state from the previous frame. Unchecking a hovered switch swaps :checked:hover for :hover, so the fill changed with no transition.\n\nAlso the off track hovered darker than idle on a dark theme (translucent --border-hover over a solid --border-secondary); hover is now a wash of --text-primary over the idle fill.","files":null}]}